                <pb facs="0386" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.48/376: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-12T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                                1920—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>866. Your 1179, August 5, 4 P.M.</p>
                <p>Department agrees with views expressed in last paragraph of your telegram and has
                    today indicated to Director of European Children’s Fund that it is Department’s
                    desire that no member of their organization remain in territory under Bolshevik
                    occupation. You may so inform Brown who will be advised directly by New York
                    Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
